{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1393296-question-about-the-tuatha","id":1393296,"title":"Question about the Tuatha?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-31T19:19:49-07:00","id":1393296,"title":"Question about the Tuatha?","content":"What general timeframe would you put the war between the Tuatha and the Fomorians that ends with the Tuatha becoming the supreme power in Ireland? The late Bronze Age (2000 BCE)? Roman times? Or some other timeframe?<br /> <br /> Just wondering. Thanks.<br /> <br /> @No One of Consequence<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T19:35:49-07:00","id":1393299,"title":"","content":"See this always confused me, the Kithain call it the war of the Trees and they seem to imply it was prehistoric times. And it was before humans came to Ireland, but I believe the Fianna helped them in it. So i would say over 8k BCE because we had to have a decent era in between Tuatha reigning and mortal Milesians colonized it. So he\u2019ll this could have been like Impergium 11k-14k era and it would still make sense. But the war wasn\u2019t limited to Ireland, but the Tuatha conquering Ireland represents them winning the War Worldwide. And Fianna arriving with the Milesians maybe even helped the Tuatha reach an agreement with mankind.<br /> <br /> The Tuatha stories like encountering the first Mages and such seem to be hella long time ago caveman days and I believe they are implied to be after they already won the War of the Trees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T19:38:07-07:00","id":1393301,"title":"","content":"Doh mixed this up with the Changeling the dreaming subforum!<br /> <br /> But a lot of the points still stand I would have it be before humans from the Iberian peninsula came. Though if you go with a Theoi dominant game you could use the theories about Ireland being colonized by humans post the Trojan War and in that case your suggested timeline is a bit closer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T19:47:35-07:00","id":1393305,"title":"","content":"That really helps. Thanks \ud83d\ude0a.<br /> <br /> Important question though<br /> <br /> I picked the late Bronze Age because that\u2019s about the time the first Celts settled in Ireland. Since the Tuatha are a Celtic pantheon, wouldn\u2019t they have arrived with the Celts and then displaced the Fomorians, who represented the pre-Celtic inhabitants of Ireland?<br /> <br /> Anthropology is not my area. Are my assumptions wrong?<br /> <br /> This would work for either Scion or Changeling since the mythic source material is the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T19:52:17-07:00","id":1393307,"title":"","content":"Your assumptions are faulty. The Tuatha were there before humans settled the island, and view the humans as interlopers.<br /> <br /> And while Scion and Changeling are both based on the same source material, they differ wildly in terms of how that source material is interpreted and to what extent they stay true to it. Changeling takes a lot more liberties with it than Scion does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-31-2020, 10:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T20:12:08-07:00","id":1393313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1393296-question-about-the-tuatha?p=1393307#post1393307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your assumptions are faulty. The Tuatha were there before humans settled the island, and view the humans as interlopers.<br /> <br /> And while Scion and Changeling are both based on the same source material, they differ wildly in terms of how that source material is interpreted and to what extent they stay true to it. Changeling takes a lot more liberties with it than Scion does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I didn\u2019t realize it was scion when I posted the first response.<br /> <br /> <br /> By Tuatha reckoning Firbholg were the beings they conquered to take Ireland, and both Tuatha and Firbholg had wars with the Fomorians. And they humans had to take Ireland from the Tuatha. A lot of Irish myth written in book form comes from a Christian perspective by attributing biblical origins to the tribes of Godbeings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T20:32:07-07:00","id":1393320,"title":"","content":"Interesting. Thank you guys.<br /> <br /> I still have trouble wrapping my head around the issue of why a human culture would take gods as their patrons who didn\u2019t particularly like them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T20:42:09-07:00","id":1393325,"title":"","content":"The relationship between the Irish and the Tuatha in Scion is not a friendly one. It's the reason why the Irish basically tiptoe around the Tuatha, referring to them as the Good Folk, being very careful whenever they interact not to offend, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T20:43:13-07:00","id":1393326,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T01:15:23-07:00","id":1393374,"title":"","content":"Hold on let me tag an expert...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"394\" data-vbnamecard=\"394\">Watcher</a> would you care to weigh in?<br /> <br /> And the relationship between the Tuatha and the Irish of centuries ago was... CONTENTIOUS, from what I know. Which to be fair is like, next to nothing. Many of the oldest stories we have of the Tuatha de Danann come from a culture that would feel very odd to us. Most of them weren't even really worshipped in the early 800s the same way we think of worshipping Gods today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T05:19:49-07:00","id":1393400,"title":"","content":"The fact that all the stories and in fact almost every single detail we have on the Tuatha comes from the pens of Christian monks and clergy at least a couple of centuries after they cease to be worshiped, though in a period when they are still believed in, makes me leary of sticking to close to the source material with the Tuatha. Not my problem in other cases;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T08:19:45-07:00","id":1393434,"title":"","content":"I mean in that case we should dismiss everything written about the \u00c6gir as well, since pretty much everything we know about them come from records written after the worship of them stopped","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T08:49:43-07:00","id":1393442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1393296-question-about-the-tuatha?p=1393400#post1393400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that all the stories and in fact almost every single detail we have on the Tuatha comes from the pens of Christian monks and clergy at least a couple of centuries after they cease to be worshiped, though in a period when they are still believed in, makes me leary of sticking to close to the source material with the Tuatha. Not my problem in other cases;-)</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be great if we had any other sources for the historical Tuatha, but sadly we don't... So the one where their solidly a part of Abrahamic Cosmology (well, to various degrees of solidity given how many things the Irish Monks and Saints at the time were indulging in that more mainland churches would have found heretical <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> The same applies to the Aesir, which is why we have so many records of their myths, but little to nothing of their actual worship <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T09:03:39-07:00","id":1393446,"title":"","content":"So you guys are saying that almost everything we know about the Tuatha is based on stuff written down by Christian monks (like the ones at Lindisfarne)?<br /> <br /> Wow. I didn\u2019t know any of that. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T09:18:04-07:00","id":1393454,"title":"","content":"Waking up today to do work on the Finn Cycle and instead I'm being thrust into the Book of Invasions to establish dates. Okay.jpg<br /> <br /> (I'm joking, I love to answer questions, this just might be long-winded, sorry in advance)<br /> <br /> So, to start with, that Changeling: the Dreaming stuff is interesting and I might go looking into that later (The War of the Trees is a <i>Welsh</i> thing, that's an interesting choice to use) for my own research into the Celts in Pop Culture, but as Eld. says there, it is totally off from the actual material. While the source material is the same, as you point out Penelope, the WoD stuff there mostly is just reusing names at random rather than using the actual material.<br /> <br /> Further, just a little bit of current research. The Celts never 'moved into' Ireland or anything like that. Through genetic analysis we know the Irish are genetically the same from modern day all the way down to the ice sheets leaving, there has been no major disruption of the population. This causes issues, no doubt, with language development and the move of Proto-Indo-European peoples and the Westward Expansion of the Celts theory which we have not resolved yet, but we're working on it. This is a <i>very</i> contentious topic academically right now, like, so contentious that I was at a talk by one of the main scholars in the field at the main formal conference for the field, and the dude beside me was <i>swearing</i> about the presenter because he disagreed. Like, this was <i>incredibly</i> heated and contentious. Just, like, to provide the context of the 'we dunno'.<br /> <br /> Normally for Scion I suggest not using actual dates and times for Pantheons because things are wishy washy. Tragically, the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 actually have a very specific time-scale for everything. We know the specific dates of all the invasions of Ireland even, and I think possibly The Second Battle of Mag Tuired, the war with the Fomorians you are talking about. See, the Irish placed their sagas and tales in the wider context of a Christian narrative, and as such, the timeline is linked up to that. For instance, the first invasion was shortly before The Flood, Conchobar mac Nessa dies when Jesus dies, and the Finn Cycle is told to Patrick.<br /> <br /> And, lastly, for sourcing of this I am using The Book of Invasions / <i>Lebor Gab\u00e1la \u00c9renn</i>, the only text that actually covers the invasion periods in detail and so on and so forth. The Annals of the Four Masters, a medieval Irish Chronicle will augment this, as it has a King List which lets us work out the dates of things. The way we can use this to establish dating is the description of the time periods that specific kings ruled and working backwards from historic kings. So, for instance, we know when king X ruled, and The Annals of the Four Masters says the probably-fictional person before him ruled for 13 years, and the one before him for 6 and so on and so forth <i>all</i> the way back to the first kings in Ireland, the Fir Bolg.<br /> <br /> So!<br /> <br /> The Fir Bolg kingship starts with Sl\u00e1ine mac Dela comes to power in 1934 BCE, with the fall of the last Fir Bolg high king (and a very good Order Titan tbh) Eochaid mac Eirc in the war with the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 who were invading to conquer Ireland is in 1897. So, we can firmly establish that the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 invaded Ireland in and around this year. Then we have the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 king list which we can look at in conjunction with The Book of Invasions to establish the events during these periods of history. We know that Lug is given temporary kingship by Nuadu for the battle with the Fomorians (it was less of a prolonged war and just one <i>really big</i> battle), so we can use this to establish the date of the battle as 1870 BCE. The three T\u00faatha D\u00e9 kings who ruled Ireland in conjunction are overthrown by the invading M\u00edlisians (who, by the by, descendants of Ramses II) in 1700 BCE.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. Those are the specific years these things happen. If you want to be <i>really</i> specific, I think The Book of Invasions gives the specific day and month for the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 invasion of Ireland as the Kalends of May, so, the first of May. Though, I'll be honest, <i>that</i> is going from memory of the opening line of the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 section in the manuscript, so I could be fucking that one up.<br /> <br /> Hope that helped!<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, yeah, everything we know about the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 come from Irish-Christian monks. Ireland arrives in the 2nd-4th century in Ireland (again, bit of a vicious debate), and the sagas are not recorded until the 8th. The story of the invasion of Ireland isn't even recorded until the 11th.<br /> <br /> Honestly, there is less alterations of the text for Christian reasons and more political reasons. The entire Ulster Cycle was doctored by the O'Neill dynasty to pull some fancy political and propagandist tricks against the previous Ulaid dynasty (see: 'Fury Destroys the World': historical strategy in Ireland's Ulster Epic), and the Fomorians were not always antagonists, but made into antagonists in roughly the 10th century as Norse-expies (see: Myth and Mythography of Cath Maige Tuired). Originally Fomorian was another name for the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 and there was no division. This is why the family trees are so intertwined, because they <i>weren't</i> two different family trees originally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 06-01-2020, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T13:11:14-07:00","id":1393499,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"394\" data-vbnamecard=\"394\">Watcher</a> wow! You know A LOT about this area. Thank you \ud83d\ude0a. I really appreciate it.<br /> <br /> The Milisians were Egyptian?<br /> <br /> What\u2019s an expy?<br /> <br /> Thanks to everyone who answered this thread. This has been amazingly helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T13:51:43-07:00","id":1393505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1393296-question-about-the-tuatha?p=1393446#post1393446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you guys are saying that almost everything we know about the Tuatha is based on stuff written down by Christian monks (like the ones at Lindisfarne)?<br /> <br /> Wow. I didn\u2019t know any of that. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may want to read the book &quot;Ireland's Immortals&quot;. Watcher, after you've read the book, will give you info on it's limits. But it is the accessible book on the subject. Look for quality used on Amazon. Unless you've got a local bookstore, then order through them and be blessed. ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 06-01-2020, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T14:00:12-07:00","id":1393509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1393296-question-about-the-tuatha?p=1393499#post1393499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> wow! You know A LOT about this area. Thank you \ud83d\ude0a. I really appreciate it.<br /> <br /> The Milisians were Egyptian?<br /> <br /> What\u2019s an expy?<br /> <br /> Thanks to everyone who answered this thread. This has been amazingly helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to local legend, all of the Irish, Scots, and Manx, are descendents of the Princess Scotia. She is always said to be Egyptian. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Welsh, Cornish, and Breton, claim descent from the royalty of Troy. This myth was taken over by the English and as late as the English Civil Wars they would call themselves &quot;Troyans.&quot; &quot;Greetings good Troyan!&quot; was a fairly normal way to say hello in London in the Tudor period.<br /> <br /> Mythic histories are charmingly daft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T14:01:04-07:00","id":1393510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1393296-question-about-the-tuatha?p=1393499#post1393499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"394\" data-vbnamecard=\"394\">Watcher</a> wow! You know A LOT about this area. Thank you \ud83d\ude0a. I really appreciate it.<br /> <br /> The Milisians were Egyptian?<br /> <br /> What\u2019s an expy?<br /> <br /> Thanks to everyone who answered this thread. This has been amazingly helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely always happy to help with the T\u00faatha D\u00e9! I am a PhD student studying Irish Saga literature, and my supervisor is... always careful about how much to say as it is such a small field and I don't strictly want to Dox myself any more than has been done before. My supervisor is one of the world experts on the Mythological Cycle, so I get a lot of exposure to the 3 Scion-relevent cycles (Mythological, Ulster, and Finn) through my own research and getting to spend time with my supervisor.<br /> <br /> The Book of Invasions claims that M\u00edl, the main ancestor of the M\u00edlisians, married the daughter of 'Pharaoh' as they passed through Egypt from the Middle East to Spain and on to Ireland for their invasion. While the book treats 'Pharaoh' as a proper name for the King of Egypt, it talks about how he is the same 'King of Egypt' who dealt with the plagues and other biblical references, so we can pin it down to Ramses II. <br /> <br /> An Expy is an abbreviation for 'exported character'. So, the Fomorians as we see them in the wars with the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 are supposed to be stand-ins or metaphors for the Norse. It is very, very overt to be honest. Seaborne raiders from islands to the north of Ireland who raid and try to put Ireland under taxation. If it was that alone it might be a shaky theory, but the fact that this characterization of them only forms when medieval Irish politics was getting super concerned about the Norse (tbh it was less the Irish getting upset because 'Irish' wasn't an identity yet. It was Connaught and Munster getting annoyed that Leinster had such strong allies in the Hiberno-Norse of Dublin and were thus connected to large trade and alliance systems IIRC) makes it pretty evident that it was mostly a political smear campaign that resulted in the Fomorians taking form.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T14:03:24-07:00","id":1393512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicjohnny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1393296-question-about-the-tuatha?p=1393434#post1393434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean in that case we should dismiss everything written about the \u00c6gir as well, since pretty much everything we know about them come from records written after the worship of them stopped</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more ambiguous. Some of the poems in the Elder Eddas might date from the Pagan period in their present form. There is debate among serious scholars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T14:36:49-07:00","id":1393517,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar857_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"857\" data-vbnamecard=\"857\">Astromancer</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"394\" data-vbnamecard=\"394\">Watcher</a> that\u2019s fascinating. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T15:04:27-07:00","id":1393527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1393296-question-about-the-tuatha?p=1393512#post1393512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's more ambiguous. Some of the poems in the Elder Eddas might date from the Pagan period in their present form. There is debate among serious scholars.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Iceland didn\u2019t have the bloody switch to Christianity the rest of Scandinavia had, they could keep their cultural history, all Snorri did was add a section about his ideas on the Aesir being the legacy of Troy.<br /> <br /> This is why the Codex Regius is useful even if it isn\u2019t truly ancient, Iceland\u2019s association with their cultural history didn\u2019t have the stigma of say Norway with their conversion to Christianity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T15:31:53-07:00","id":1393534,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> is it relevant that Iceland was (sort of) a democracy when the rest of the Scandinavian countries were monarchies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T15:51:08-07:00","id":1393538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1393296-question-about-the-tuatha?p=1393534#post1393534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> is it relevant that Iceland was (sort of) a democracy when the rest of the Scandinavian countries were monarchies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I am certain that you've put your finger on the key fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T16:00:32-07:00","id":1393542,"title":"","content":"Awesome \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T20:03:36-07:00","id":1393571,"title":"","content":"They became Christian peacefully and things like Althings allow for grievances and concerns to be heard. So there was a lot less stigma about the old faith of the their ancestors. I've heard they also have some older bits of the faith and may have contributed to things because they live on an Island of extremes, both snow and volcanoes, and so they had a lot to draw on with their takes on Muspelheim/Jotunheim/Niflheim. Much different then Kings turning Christian and their kingdom following suit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T00:38:05-07:00","id":1393586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1393296-question-about-the-tuatha?p=1393454#post1393454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fir Bolg kingship starts with Sl\u00e1ine mac Dela comes to power in 1934 BCE, with the fall of the last Fir Bolg high king (and a very good Order Titan tbh) Eochaid mac Eirc in the war with the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 who were invading to conquer Ireland is in 1897. So, we can firmly establish that the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 invaded Ireland in and around this year.</div> </div> </div> </div>... this struck me as very odd, so I googled and ended up browsing Wikipedia for a bit. It ended up being an interesting excursion into seeing how the concept of kingship might emergently solidify over a period of time while people figured out what they really wanted from him in practice. Seeing the length of each reign made it make a sudden amount of sense.<br /> <br /> Thanks for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T01:51:59-07:00","id":1393595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1393296-question-about-the-tuatha?p=1393510#post1393510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Absolutely always happy to help with the T\u00faatha D\u00e9! I am a PhD student studying Irish Saga literature, and my supervisor is... always careful about how much to say as it is such a small field and I don't strictly want to Dox myself any more than has been done before. My supervisor is one of the world experts on the Mythological Cycle, so I get a lot of exposure to the 3 Scion-relevent cycles (Mythological, Ulster, and Finn) through my own research and getting to spend time with my supervisor.<br /> <br /> The Book of Invasions claims that M\u00edl, the main ancestor of the M\u00edlisians, married the daughter of 'Pharaoh' as they passed through Egypt from the Middle East to Spain and on to Ireland for their invasion. While the book treats 'Pharaoh' as a proper name for the King of Egypt, it talks about how he is the same 'King of Egypt' who dealt with the plagues and other biblical references, so we can pin it down to Ramses II.<br /> <br /> An Expy is an abbreviation for 'exported character'. So, the Fomorians as we see them in the wars with the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 are supposed to be stand-ins or metaphors for the Norse. It is very, very overt to be honest. Seaborne raiders from islands to the north of Ireland who raid and try to put Ireland under taxation. If it was that alone it might be a shaky theory, but the fact that this characterization of them only forms when medieval Irish politics was getting super concerned about the Norse (tbh it was less the Irish getting upset because 'Irish' wasn't an identity yet. It was Connaught and Munster getting annoyed that Leinster had such strong allies in the Hiberno-Norse of Dublin and were thus connected to large trade and alliance systems IIRC) makes it pretty evident that it was mostly a political smear campaign that resulted in the Fomorians taking form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for sharing your knowledge, Watcher! This is all really quite interesting. If you're still taking questions: can you comment on whether the Biblical connections and allusions in the Irish mytho-history are made for any discernible thematic reasons or if they are just more general gestures like &quot;yeah, our history is very important because it is connected to Biblical history&quot;? What I mean is, I can work out why the first settlement of Ireland is attributed to a daughter of Noah - that conveys a very ancient history, at the very least. But is there, for instance, a reason why they would want to claim descent from Pharaoh, who really doesn't seem like a very pleasant figure to be descended from? Or is that just a general claim to a sufficiently 'exotic' royal lineage?<br /> <br /> Also, to everybody else, let me do some shameless promotion of somebody else's work: for those of you who haven't noticed, Watcher has written an excellent expansion to the Tuatha D\u00e9 that is available <i>for free</i> on the nexus! You can find the link in their signature. For me personally, reading Watcher's <i>Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</i> has made the Tuatha one of my favourite pantheons in Scion and re-contextualises a lot of things said in the Hero write-up in an interesting and (I assume) more myth-accurate way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Pantheon:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1d6MGe0uK0nLsOABBu3YymfU-7gS7Nwur/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Th\u1ea7n of Vietnam</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25842-mr-wopsle","name":"Mr Wopsle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25842_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T09:10:40-07:00","id":1393651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Wopsle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1393296-question-about-the-tuatha?p=1393595#post1393595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for sharing your knowledge, Watcher! This is all really quite interesting. If you're still taking questions: can you comment on whether the Biblical connections and allusions in the Irish mytho-history are made for any discernible thematic reasons or if they are just more general gestures like &quot;yeah, our history is very important because it is connected to Biblical history&quot;? What I mean is, I can work out why the first settlement of Ireland is attributed to a daughter of Noah - that conveys a very ancient history, at the very least. But is there, for instance, a reason why they would want to claim descent from Pharaoh, who really doesn't seem like a very pleasant figure to be descended from? Or is that just a general claim to a sufficiently 'exotic' royal lineage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, there's a lot of potential answers for that one. Let's see.<br /> <br /> So, first and foremost, medieval Europe was particularly concerned with establishing themselves to the past to foster legitimacy, political authority, and to create a connection to this fabled past of Rome and the rest of them. This results in a lot of, let's say, 'standard practices' in attempts to claim connections to the past. For instance, the Irish (along with: literally everyone else) claimed to be descendants of Troy, from Brutus of Troy, and therefore had similar authority to Rome who was also founded by a Trojan survivor. The Irish also claimed to be one of the lost tribes of Israel, that they had knowledge of God before the coming of Jesus (this shows up in the Acallam where Finn and his <i>f\u00edana</i> are said to have realized that an all powerful God must exist after seeing a huge act of divine intervention based off the ground swallowing up the golden calf in the bible), and a bunch of other stuff. They wrote their own fanfic of the Odyssey and the Iliad where Ireland is an important plot element, tons of stuff like that.<br /> <br /> This has a lot to do with how medieval Europe understood history. We see history as something that is true, medieval Europe saw history more like a fable. It was what it could be, not what it was. And through what it could be, it was.<br /> <br /> For wider reasons that Irish material was incorporated into a wider Christian world, we have to see that Ireland was a particularly odd situation in terms of Christianity. They were converted, and then isolated when Britain suddenly had a bunch of Germanic tribes in it. This resulted in Ireland wandering off and doing their own thing. King-Abbots, Druid-Monks, Warrior-Monks, the professions of Christianity were just slotted into the existing system. And, then, when the sagas were to be recorded, these people didn't 'taint' or 'twist' the stories, they loved these stories. If they wanted to twist or taint them they did a pretty shitty job at it. They recorded these stories and they labored to the extent of quite honestly flat out heresy to make their stories and traditions work in a Christian world. This is why the Otherworld Islands exist. The Otherworld was originally 'down', but with Christianity, 'down' was already occupied. And 'up' wasn't an option, and 'here', well, that's where the monks lived so clearly the Otherworld wasn't here, so it had to be shifted to 'over there'. Instead of associating the Otherworld with Hell, they found a way to make it work. They claimed the T\u00faatha D\u00e9 were 'unfallen humans' which is.... <i>huge</i> in terms of 'that's not a thing'.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. That's where these Christian elements come from. And, the reason they attribute the settlement to Noah's daughter is that she was as far back as they could go. You can't have people settling before that point, because everyone dies. (At least, most of everyone. Ireland has several people who survive the flood through various tricks.) So, they went back as far as possible. The reason they claimed descent from Pharaoh even though he wasn't a great dude by the bible was that they wanted a connection to that world of the bible. He was a king, so marrying his daughter seemed like a solid story. So, they went with it. Less 'exotic' and more 'placing ourselves in the setting of our religion' and 'well he has to marry someone politically important'.<br /> <br /> So, long story short, these elements are because they as Christians wanted to keep their stories and understood them in the new worldview.<br /> <br /> Now, the political stuff, <i>that</i> is actual doctoring with an intent and will behind it, but the sagas themselves were just a culture recording their stories.<br /> <br /> Edit: As pointed out by a friend of mine, M\u00edl marrying into the family of Pharaoh means they're in the same kin-group as Moses and <i>that</i> is a big deal from their perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 06-02-2020, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T12:34:00-07:00","id":1393823,"title":"","content":"Thank you so much! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Pantheon:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1d6MGe0uK0nLsOABBu3YymfU-7gS7Nwur/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Th\u1ea7n of Vietnam</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25842-mr-wopsle","name":"Mr Wopsle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25842_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T05:47:05-07:00","id":1397963,"title":"","content":"Traditional Irish myth-history placed the events firmly in the Bronze Age (anywhere from ca. 1300-ca. 1900 BCE, depending on whose chronology you like). More information here: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tuatha_D%C3%A9_Danann#Tuatha_D%C3%A9_Danann_High_Kings_of_Ireland\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tuatha...ngs_of_Ireland</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;</span>Explanations exist; they have existed for all time; there is always a well-known solution to every human problem \u2014 neat, plausible, and wrong.<span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;<br /> - H.L. Mencken</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/467-bob-the-skull","name":"Bob the Skull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T06:01:05-07:00","id":1397966,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/467-bob-the-skull\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar467_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"467\" data-vbnamecard=\"467\">Bob the Skull</a> thank you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T12:42:32-07:00","id":1398040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1393296-question-about-the-tuatha?p=1393446#post1393446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you guys are saying that almost everything we know about the Tuatha is based on stuff written down by Christian monks (like the ones at Lindisfarne)?<br /> <br /> Wow. I didn\u2019t know any of that. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's true. There just wasn't an extensive written record in Ireland before that time (ogham texts are typically very short), and the mythological and historical traditions were entirely oral. That means there is the potential for alterations and biases in what was eventually written down, but we do what we can with what we have, yes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;</span>Explanations exist; they have existed for all time; there is always a well-known solution to every human problem \u2014 neat, plausible, and wrong.<span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;<br /> - H.L. Mencken</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/467-bob-the-skull","name":"Bob the Skull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}